body:
Test coverage is missing for the interaction between summary features and grouped views. Since the implementation only renders summaries in non-grouped mode (line 1270-1275 in ObjectGrid.tsx), there should be tests verifying: (1) that summaries are not displayed when grouping is enabled, or (2) that summaries are correctly aggregated per-group if that's the intended behavior. Add test cases covering the grouped + summary scenario.
```suggestion
  });

  it('does not render column summaries when grouping is enabled', async () => {
    renderGrid({
      columns: [
        { field: 'name', label: 'Name' },
        { field: 'amount', label: 'Amount', type: 'number', summary: { type: 'sum' } },
      ],
      // Enable grouping on an existing field; summaries should not render in grouped mode
      groupBy: ['name'],
      data: { provider: 'value', items: numericData },
    });

    await waitFor(() => {
      expect(screen.getByText('Name')).toBeInTheDocument();
    });

    // When grouping is enabled, the global column summary footer should not be rendered
    expect(screen.queryByTestId('column-summary-footer')).not.toBeInTheDocument();
  });
```

Test coverage is missing for summary aggregation behavior with pagination and filtering. The current tests only verify summaries with static data arrays. Add test cases that verify: (1) whether summaries aggregate over all data or only visible/filtered data when pagination is enabled, and (2) how summaries behave when filters are applied. This is important to document the expected behavior given the potential bug identified in line 364 of ObjectGrid.tsx.
```suggestion
  });

  it('aggregates summaries across all pages when pagination is enabled', async () => {
    const items = [
      { id: 1, name: 'Row 1', score: 1 },
      { id: 2, name: 'Row 2', score: 2 },
      { id: 3, name: 'Row 3', score: 3 },
      { id: 4, name: 'Row 4', score: 4 },
      { id: 5, name: 'Row 5', score: 5 },
    ];

    renderGrid({
      columns: [
        { field: 'name', label: 'Name', summary: 'count' },
        { field: 'score', label: 'Score', type: 'number', summary: { type: 'sum' } },
      ],
      data: { provider: 'value', items },
      pagination: {
        pageSize: 2,
        enabled: true,
      },
    });

    await waitFor(() => {
      expect(screen.getByText('Name')).toBeInTheDocument();
    });

    const footer = screen.getByTestId('column-summary-footer');
    expect(footer).toBeInTheDocument();

    // Even though only a subset of rows are visible on the current page,
    // summaries should aggregate over the full dataset.
    expect(screen.getByTestId('summary-name')).toHaveTextContent('Count: 5');
    expect(screen.getByTestId('summary-score')).toHaveTextContent('Sum: 15');
  });

  it('updates summaries based on filtered data (across all pages)', async () => {
    const items = [
      { id: 1, name: 'Row 1', status: 'active', score: 1 },
      { id: 2, name: 'Row 2', status: 'inactive', score: 2 },
      { id: 3, name: 'Row 3', status: 'active', score: 3 },
      { id: 4, name: 'Row 4', status: 'inactive', score: 4 },
      { id: 5, name: 'Row 5', status: 'active', score: 4 },
    ];

    renderGrid({
      columns: [
        { field: 'name', label: 'Name', summary: 'count' },
        { field: 'score', label: 'Score', type: 'number', summary: { type: 'sum' } },
        { field: 'status', label: 'Status' },
      ],
      data: { provider: 'value', items },
      filters: {
        provider: 'value',
        items: [
          {
            field: 'status',
            operator: 'eq',
            value: 'active',
          },
        ],
      },
      pagination: {
        pageSize: 2,
        enabled: true,
      },
    });

    await waitFor(() => {
      expect(screen.getByText('Name')).toBeInTheDocument();
    });

    const footer = screen.getByTestId('column-summary-footer');
    expect(footer).toBeInTheDocument();

    // Only rows with status "active" should be included in the summaries.
    // There are 3 active rows with scores 1, 3, and 4.
    expect(screen.getByTestId('summary-name')).toHaveTextContent('Count: 3');
    expect(screen.getByTestId('summary-score')).toHaveTextContent('Sum: 8');
  });
```
